{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, this screen's gone blank again. Right. What brings you in today?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Um, it's the burning when I wee. That's why I came.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Burning when you wee. Say it once more, I was in the wrong window.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): It stings. When I pass urine, yeah.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long for?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Four days, I reckon. Err, might've been Sunday. I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Monday arvo, when I came on shift. Four days, yes.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (DOCTOR): Going more often than usual?",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. Heaps more. Um, up at night, twice I think.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Three times last night. The loo door sticks so I hear every trip.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Was it three? I don't know, doctor. A lot, anyway.",
  "[SEG0012] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any discharge from the penis?",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nothing like that.",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (DOCTOR): Back pain at all?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah, low down. An ache. Not sharp or anything, just across the bottom.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (DOCTOR): One side or both? Sorry, the mouse just died.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor. Maybe a bit more on the left. Not sure.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (CAREGIVER): He's had a hand pressed on his lower back since Tuesday.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any fever? Shakes?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): A bit warm. Not proper sick. I don't know.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I did the thermometer this morning, before the taxi. 37.8. He grumbled the whole time.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (DOCTOR): 37.8, so only mild. Been travelling? Overseas, up the coast?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Haven't been anywhere. Just the flat.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): And the bowels, any change there? Tummy pain?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Bowels are fine. Tummy's alright.",
  "[SEG0026] person_1 (DOCTOR): What medicines are you taking?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): Panadol, now and then, for the ache. And a blood pressure tablet. I don't know the name, doctor.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (CAREGIVER): It's perindopril, five milligrams, every morning.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah. I do miss it some mornings. Maybe a couple of times a week. I don't know.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): Couple of times a week. And the dose, say it again, the screen wiped it.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Five mg, mornings. Oh, and that's not the metformin. My husband takes metformin for his sugar. Both packs live in the same drawer, I nearly grabbed his. Not yours, love.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah nah. I don't take his stuff.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any reactions to medicines? Antibiotics, rashes, swelling?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): No, never. I have taken penicillin and everything. Amoxil years ago, for a chest infection. Took the whole pack, no drama.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): So no allergies. Amoxil was fine, no rash. Any old test results floating around? Cursor's stuck, go on.",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): They did a PSA at the other clinic. They said it was borderline. I don't know the number, doctor. Wasn't written down.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): Borderline, no figure. Sounds like a urine infection, but the lab has to confirm it. We'll get a urine sample to the lab today. If it grows something I'll start trimethaprim, not before we see it. Come back in a week, and sooner if the fever climbs or you can't pass urine. Try not to skip the perindopril.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I'll stick his webster pack by the kettle so the morning tablet actually gets taken. And I'll check it's his pack, not my husband's.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Yep. Jar's on the front desk. Off you go."
 ],
